WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:04.300
Compare databases. Staging, production, and every client database.

2
00:00:04.600 --> 00:00:14.700
We ship one database to many clients. Soon nobody knows which client has which tables, which procedure is missing, or which schema never shipped.

3
00:00:15.200 --> 00:00:18.000
The easy fix: compare them with SchemaScope.

4
00:00:18.600 --> 00:00:21.200
Step 1: First, pick the database you trust.

5
00:00:21.600 --> 00:00:25.000
Step 2: Add every target: QA and eight clients.

6
00:00:25.600 --> 00:00:29.400
Step 3: Press Compare. All nine at once, in about a second.

7
00:00:30.200 --> 00:00:33.000
Step 4: Every client gets a score, worst first.

8
00:00:33.600 --> 00:00:40.800
Step 5: See what is missing. Client04 never got the support schema. Client03 lacks tables and procedures.

9
00:00:41.400 --> 00:00:44.600
Step 6: Open any object to see the exact lines.

10
00:00:45.250 --> 00:00:48.600
Step 7: Create scripts that fix it, each checked offline first.

11
00:00:49.000 --> 00:00:53.400
Step 8: New in 1.2: write mode. Type the name to apply.

12
00:00:54.600 --> 00:00:59.200
Step 8: Client05 goes to 100%. Protected servers are refused.

13
00:00:59.600 --> 00:01:05.000
Stop comparing in pairs. Free at schemascope.shadowmark.in
